card.statement:
Suppose that the simple normal crossings divisor $\D\subset \X$ is the degeneracy divisor of a log symplectic Poisson structure. Then the following identity holds in the cohomology ring of $\X$:

\begin{align}
\ch(\tshf{\X})-\ch(\cotshf{\X}) = 2\sum_{j=1}^k \sinh\, [\D_j],
\end{align}

where $\ch(\tshf{\X})$ and $\ch(\cotshf{\X})$ are the Chern characters of the tangent and cotangent bundles.
